  "question": {
    "text": "Consider <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;boxes, where each box contains <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> red balls and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> blue balls. Assume that all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn></math> balls are distinct. In how many different ways can <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> balls be chosen from these <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> boxes so that from each box at least one red ball and one blue ball are chosen?",
    "image": null
  },
